How to Run

Clone or download this repository.

Place academic_survival_longitudinal.csv in the same directory as
the notebook.

Install the required Python libraries.

Open Module_6_Student_Dropout_Prediction_Final.ipynb in Jupyter
Notebook or JupyterLab.

Restart the kernel and run all cells from top to bottom.

Example installation command:

pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn scikit-learn jupyter

Conclusion

The project demonstrates an end-to-end data science workflow for
analyzing student academic survival and the dropout target.

Random Forest achieved higher overall accuracy, while Logistic
Regression achieved substantially higher recall for class 1. The
comparison highlights the trade-off between identifying more
minority-class cases and reducing false-positive predictions.

The models should be treated as analytical and predictive tools. Further
validation and model improvement would be required before considering
use in a real student-support environment.

